{"name":"Ravine","hex":"#d3cec7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ravine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep narrow valley or gorge in the earth's surface worn by running water."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of ravin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ravine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ravine","blocks":[{"text":"A ravine is a landform that is narrower than a canyon and is often the product of streambank erosion. Ravines are typically classified as larger in scale than gullies, although smaller than valleys. A ravine may also be called a cleuch, dene or dean, dell, ghout (Nevis), gill or ghyll, glen,  goyle, gorge, kloof, or chine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Wawoz_homole2.jpg/330px-Wawoz_homole2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ravine"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/%D0%95%D0%BD%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%85%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD%2C_%D0%A8%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B5_%D1%83%D1%89%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B5_%D1%81%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%85%D1%83_%289%29.jpg/500px-%D0%95%D0%BD%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%85%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD%2C_%D0%A8%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B5_%D1%83%D1%89%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B5_%D1%81%D0%B2%D0%B5%D1%80%D1%85%D1%83_%289%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/%D0%95%D0%BD%D0%B1%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%88%D0%B8%D0%BA%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B0%D1%85%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%B8%D0%B9_%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BE%D0%BD%2C_%D0%A8%D0%B8%D0%BD%D1%82%D1%83%D1%80%D0%B3%D0%B5%D0%BD%D1%81%D0%BA%D0%BE%D0%B5_%D1%83%D1%89%D0%B5%D0%BB%D1%8C%D0%B5_%